.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH setools-mcp 1 "2026-10-07" "SETools" "SETools Manual"
.SH NAME
setools-mcp \- run the SETools Model Context Protocol server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setools-mcp
.RB [ \-\-policy
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-transport
.BR stdio | http ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR ADDRESS ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setools-mcp
exposes SETools SELinux policy-analysis tools through Model Context Protocol.
The default stdio transport is suitable for a client-managed local process.
The HTTP transport provides a persistent Streamable HTTP server.
.PP
Supplying
.B \-\-config
defaults to HTTP transport and configures startup settings, operational routes,
session cache, and policy provider. An explicit transport setting may select stdio.
Explicit command-line policy, transport, host, and port arguments override file values.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-policy " PATH"
Use PATH as the default local SELinux policy, overriding the configured default policy.
.TP
.BI \-\-transport " TRANSPORT"
Use
.B stdio
or
.B http
transport, overriding the configured transport.
The default is stdio without a configuration file and HTTP with one.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ADDRESS"
Bind the HTTP server to ADDRESS, overriding the configured host.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Bind the HTTP server to PORT, overriding the configured port.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Load reusable server and policy-provider settings from PATH.
Omitted command-line options preserve file values.
The file must be valid even when a value would be overridden.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable informational logging.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging and Python warnings.
.SH CONFIGURATION
See
.I docs/MCP-CONFIG.md
and
.I docs/mcp-http.ini
for the configuration format and an Azure DevOps Universal Package example.
.PP
The
.B [server]
section supports
.BR transport ,
.BR default_policy ,
.BR name ,
and
.B instructions
alongside binding, route, request-protection, authentication, local-path, cache, and
resource-limit settings.
Instructions may use indented INI continuation lines.
.SH SECURITY
Local paths are allowed by default only for stdio transport.
Hosted deployments should keep local paths disabled, configure exact Host and Origin allowlists
with
.BR "host_origin_protection = true" ,
and run behind an appropriate HTTPS network edge.
Authentication is supplied through a FastMCP authentication provider.
The provider is responsible for token validation, authorization challenges, and protected
resource metadata.
An HTTP server with local paths disabled refuses to start without an authentication provider
unless
.B allow_unauthenticated
is set; set it only when an authenticating reverse proxy restricts access.
.PP
Readiness responses report only check names and states; details are logged.
When local paths are disabled, tool error details are masked, policy metadata omits local
filesystem paths, and query result and analysis depth limits are enforced.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR seinfo (1),
.BR sesearch (1),
.BR sediff (1)
